"The prognosis is influenced by several factors. Contributing elements include preoperative PSA of 6.2 and pathological T3a disease with extraprostatic extension noted on prostatectomy. Countervailing findings are negative surgical margins, no seminal vesicle invasion, absence of lymphovascular invasion, and no documented lymph node metastasis. The biopsy-to-prostatectomy comparison is limited as the Gleason pattern and ISUP grade report from the initial biopsy are missing. Nodal status was assessed via specimen analysis, which reported no metastasis. Information regarding postoperative PSA levels and their subsequent trajectory would significantly revise this prognosis. The fixed estimated horizon is 62.79 months. This represents expected follow-up without an event, not a known recurrence date. The sensitivity range is 50.23–75.35 months; its coverage has not been validated."
